<title>CANADA: Talisman sees cash flow rising in 1996.</title>
<headline>Talisman sees cash flow rising in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Talisman Energy Inc expects per share cash flow of between C$6.25 to C$6.45 in 1996, depending on how oil prices end up this year, Robert Mitchell, vice-president of Canadian operations, told an energy conference on Monday.</p>
<p>The cash flow estimate is up from C$5.21 a share in 1995.</p>
<p>Mitchell said Talisman was confident about its growth strategy, which is based on a strong focus on proven reserves and the desire to operate the projects in which it is involved.</p>
</text>
